menu "esp-vim USB keyboards"

    config ESP_VIM_USB_KBD
        bool "USB keyboards (USB host)"
        depends on SOC_USB_OTG_SUPPORTED
        default n
        help
            Keyboards on the chip's USB host port -- the Tab5's USB-A --
            typed as Bluetooth ones are (components/esp_kbd). Boot-protocol
            keyboards are asked for their boot reports; others are read
            through their report descriptors. Hubs and several keyboards at
            once work as the USB Host Library allows.

endmenu
